{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc | sed -n '1,260p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '450,610p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.link\n     2\t  \"The REPL's linker-side composition (yin.vm.linker.md sections 6.1 and 9,\n     3\t   M5): the interpreter box of the four-stream topology.\n     4\t\n     5\t   The shell composes the link pair per VM (`yin.repl/make-session`) and\n     6\t   the content pair per content source; this namespace owns the second\n     7\t   and answers what the first receives.  One serve round reads every link\n     8\t   request the interpreter has not yet seen, resolves each by name\n     9\t   through the composition's name environment -- the snapshot the host\n    10\t   supplies, an authority fold (`yin.vm.linker.authority/name-environment`)\n    11\t   reduced to `name -> manifest address` -- and links the manifest's\n    12\t   image over the content pair, appending the response the requesting\n    13\t   task correlates on (section 7.2, steps 5 to 6).\n    14\t\n    15\t   Step 5b is deferred: the obligations travel on the response and the\n    16\t   receiving task's engine discharges them against its live state\n    17\t   (section 7.2, step 7), so the interpreter passes\n    18\t   `:defer-discharge` to `link-manifest` and discharges nothing here.\n    19\t\n    20\t   Liveness is the composition's (section 6.3, D6): an attempt serves the\n    21\t   content pair for at most `attempt-budget` drive rounds and then\n    22\t   reports the link `:pending` -- nothing is appended, the request is\n    23\t   re-read and re-attempted on a later round, and `abandon` is the\n    24\t   shell's.  No clock, no atom, no global: every input is an argument or\n    25\t   a composition value, and every outcome is plain data.\"\n    26\t  (:require [dao.jing.content :as content]\n    27\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    29\t            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]))\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t(def pair-capacity\n    33\t  \"Declared capacity of each link-pair medium, in elements.  The shell\n    34\t   appends one request per require, and a response medium a receiver\n    35\t   never drains answers `gap` (an evicted request is never re-read), so\n    36\t   the bound is generous and the eviction it guards against is a host\n    37\t   assembly defect, not an operating condition.\"\n    38\t  1024)\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(def content-capacity\n    42\t  \"Declared capacity of each content-pair medium, in elements.  One\n    43\t   attempt's traffic is a handful of requests; the media persist across\n    44\t   attempts and every attempt mints its cursors at their newest end, so\n    45\t   an old element is never read again.\"\n    46\t  1024)\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(def attempt-budget\n    50\t  \"Drive rounds one link attempt may spend before it reports `:pending`.\n    51\t   A local pair answers within a few rounds per content request, so the\n    52\t   budget is reached only by a content source that never answers.\"\n    53\t  64)\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(def serve-steps\n    57\t  \"Server advances one drive round performs at most.  Each answers at\n    58\t   least one waiting content request, so a local pair drains in a bound\n    59\t   number of rounds.\"\n    60\t  32)\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(def serve-budget\n    64\t  \"Link requests one serve round answers, in request order.  It exceeds\n    65\t   what one evaluation's requires can enqueue, so a round that spends it\n    66\t   is answering a queue the shell did not write.\"\n    67\t  64)\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(def formats\n    71\t  \"The six format records a serving composition holds (sections 5 and\n    72\t   8.1): the four execution formats a requesting kernel names, and the\n    73\t   two the manifest flow fetches internally.\"\n    74\t  (into {}\n    75\t        (map (fn [r] [(:format r) r]))\n    76\t        [linker/ast-format linker/semantic-format linker/stack-format\n    77\t         linker/register-format linker/manifest-format\n    78\t         linker/record-format]))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- medium\n    82\t  [capacity]\n    83\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    84\t    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    85\t                   ring/capacity-key capacity})))\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(defn- newest\n    89\t  [handle]\n    90\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-newest)))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn make-pair\n    94\t  \"The link pair of one session (section 6.1): the request and response\n    95\t   media, and the interpreter's own request cursor, minted before any\n    96\t   request exists.\"\n    97\t  []\n    98\t  (let [requests (medium pair-capacity)\n    99\t        responses (medium pair-capacity)]\n   100\t    {:requests requests\n   101\t     :responses responses\n   102\t     :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   103\t               (stream/cursor requests stream/anchor-oldest))}))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn composition\n   107\t  \"The content side of the shell's link composition, from the host's\n   108\t   creation options.  `content-store` is a `dao.jing` byte-store handle\n   109\t   served in process over its own ring-buffer content pair (the\n   110\t   single-process and durable-local rows of section 6.1);\n   111\t   `content-client` is the linker's content-pair client map\n   112\t   `{:requests w :answers r :cursor c}` on a connection whose far end\n   113\t   serves content (the remote-content row), and the drive then only\n   114\t   steps the linker, the server running elsewhere (section 6.4).  A\n   115\t   content source is optional: with none, every link stays `:pending`\n   116\t   and says so.  Supplying both is a composition defect.\"\n   117\t  [{:keys [name-env content-store content-client]}]\n   118\t  (when (and content-store content-client)\n   119\t    (throw (ex-info \"content-store and content-client are exclusive\"\n   120\t                    {:content-store content-store})))\n   121\t  {:name-env (or name-env {})\n   122\t   :content (cond\n   123\t              content-store\n   124\t              {:kind :local\n   125\t               :store content-store\n   126\t               :requests (medium content-capacity)\n   127\t               :responses (medium content-capacity)}\n   128\t\n   129\t              content-client\n   130\t              {:kind :remote, :client content-client}\n   131\t\n   132\t              :else nil)})\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t;; =============================================================================\n   136\t;; One link attempt\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t\n   139\t(defn- budget-spent?\n   140\t  \"Whether `e` is the pending signal an exhausted attempt budget throws.\"\n   141\t  [e]\n   142\t  (true? (get (ex-data e) ::budget)))\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn- budget!\n   146\t  [st]\n   147\t  (when (>= (or (::round st) 0) attempt-budget)\n   148\t    (throw (ex-info \"Link attempt budget exhausted\" {::budget true}))))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t(defn- drain-server\n   152\t  \"Answer what is waiting on the content pair from the store, in at most\n   153\t   `serve-steps` serve-step advances, and return the successor server\n   154\t   cursor.\"\n   155\t  [store requests responses cursor]\n   156\t  (loop [cursor cursor\n   157\t         left serve-steps]\n   158\t    (if (zero? left)\n   159\t      cursor\n   160\t      (let [cursor' (content/serve-step store requests cursor\n   161\t                                        responses serve-steps)]\n   162\t        (if (= cursor cursor')\n   163\t          cursor\n   164\t          (recur cursor' (dec left)))))))\n   165\t\n   166\t\n   167\t(defn- attempt-runtime\n   168\t  \"The link runtime of one attempt (section 6.4): `:state` over the\n   169\t   content pair, `:drive` the composition's driver.  Both of the pair's\n   170\t   cursors are minted before the attempt's first append -- `:newest`\n   171\t   observes next arrival -- so nothing of an earlier attempt is read\n   172\t   again and nothing of this one is skipped.  The drive counts its\n   173\t   rounds and holds the server cursor on the linker state itself, so an\n   174\t   attempt that exhausts `attempt-budget` throws the pending signal and\n   175\t   the caller reports the link `:pending` -- nothing on the pair was\n   176\t   concluded.\"\n   177\t  [source]\n   178\t  (let [content (:content source)]\n   179\t    (case (:kind content)\n   180\t      :local\n   181\t      (let [requests (:requests content)\n   182\t            responses (:responses content)\n   183\t            server0 (newest requests)]\n   184\t        {:state (linker/link-state\n   185\t                  {:content {:requests requests\n   186\t                             :answers responses\n   187\t                             :cursor (newest responses)}\n   188\t                   :formats formats})\n   189\t         :drive (fn [st]\n   190\t                  (budget! st)\n   191\t                  (assoc st\n   192\t                         ::round (inc (or (::round st) 0))\n   193\t                         ::server (drain-server (:store content) requests\n   194\t                                                responses\n   195\t                                                (or (::server st)\n   196\t                                                    server0))))})\n   197\t\n   198\t      :remote\n   199\t      {:state (linker/link-state {:content (:client content)\n   200\t                                  :formats formats})\n   201\t       :drive (fn [st]\n   202\t                (budget! st)\n   203\t                (assoc st ::round (inc (or (::round st) 0))))})))\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(defn- attempt\n   207\t  \"Link one resolved name to its manifest image, or `::pending`.  The\n   208\t   requester's contract and name travel as `link-manifest` expects them;\n   209\t   step 5b is deferred to the receiving task.\"\n   210\t  [source request address]\n   211\t  (try\n   212\t    (let [res (linker/link-manifest (attempt-runtime source)\n   213\t                                    address\n   214\t                                    (:yin.link/format request)\n   215\t                                    {}\n   216\t                                    {:contract (:yin.link/contract request)\n   217\t                                     :name (:yin.link/name request)\n   218\t                                     :defer-discharge true})]\n   219\t      (if (linker/ok? res)\n   220\t        {:status :ok\n   221\t         :image {:value (:value res)}\n   222\t         :manifest (:manifest res)\n   223\t         :obligations (:obligations res)}\n   224\t        res))\n   225\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   226\t      (when-not (budget-spent? e) (throw e))\n   227\t      ::pending)))\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn- answer\n   231\t  \"The response body for one link request, or `::pending` when nothing\n   232\t   this round can answer it: no content source, or an attempt that spent\n   233\t   its budget.  A request that is not by name is refused: the\n   234\t   interpreter serves what the shell's own VMs send, the by-name\n   235\t   manifest requests of section 7.2, and nothing else.\"\n   236\t  [source request]\n   237\t  (let [name (:yin.link/name request)]\n   238\t    (cond\n   239\t      (nil? (:content source)) ::pending\n   240\t\n   241\t      (nil? name)\n   242\t      {:status :refused, :reason :invalid-request,\n   243\t       :defect :yin.repl/name-required}\n   244\t\n   245\t      :else\n   246\t      (if-let [address (get (:name-env source) name)]\n   247\t        (attempt source request address)\n   248\t        {:status :refused, :reason :absent, :name name}))))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn- respond!\n   252\t  \"Append `body` under the request's id on the response stream.  Returns\n   253\t   true when it landed, so the interpreter's cursor advances past the\n   254\t   request only then; a refused append leaves it to be re-read.\"\n   255\t  [pair request body]\n   256\t  (let [o (stream/append! (:responses pair)\n   257\t                          (assoc body :yin.link/id (:yin.link/id request)))]\n   258\t    (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome o))))\n   259\t\n   260\t\n   450\t             (filterv #(empty? (:waiting %)) pubs))])))\n   451\t\n   452\t\n   453\t;; =============================================================================\n   454\t;; Loading a published index\n   455\t;; =============================================================================\n   456\t\n   457\t(defn- probing\n   458\t  \"`handle` whose miss throws naming the missing address, so an index\n   459\t   walk says what to fetch next.\"\n   460\t  [handle]\n   461\t  (let [absent #?(:cljd (Object.) :clj (Object.) :cljs (js-obj))]\n   462\t    {:get-bytes-fn (fn [address _not-found]\n   463\t                     (let [v ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address absent)]\n   464\t                       (if (identical? absent v)\n   465\t                         (throw (ex-info \"missing\" {::missing address}))\n   466\t                         v)))\n   467\t     :put-bytes-fn (fn [_ _] (throw (ex-info \"read only\" {})))\n   468\t     :close-fn (fn [] nil)}))\n   469\t\n   470\t\n   471\t(defn- missing-in\n   472\t  [e]\n   473\t  (loop [e e]\n   474\t    (when e\n   475\t      (or (get (ex-data e) ::missing)\n   476\t          (recur (ex-cause e))))))\n   477\t\n   478\t\n   479\t(defn index-datoms\n   480\t  \"The EAVT datoms of the covered index `manifest-address` names in\n   481\t   `handle`, walked whole: `dao.space.index/read-manifest`, then every\n   482\t   index root it names, each of which must cover exactly the manifest's\n   483\t   `:count` datoms.  Throws on a missing blob or an invalid index.\"\n   484\t  [handle manifest-address]\n   485\t  (let [manifest (index/read-manifest handle manifest-address)\n   486\t        walked (into {}\n   487\t                     (map (fn [[k root]]\n   488\t                            [k (vec (index/walk-index-datoms handle root))]))\n   489\t                     (:indexes manifest))]\n   490\t    (doseq [[k datoms] walked]\n   491\t      (when-not (= (:count manifest) (count datoms))\n   492\t        (throw (ex-info (str \"the \" (name k) \" index covers \" (count datoms)\n   493\t                             \" datoms, not the manifest's \" (:count manifest))\n   494\t                        {:index k :manifest manifest-address}))))\n   495\t    (or (:eavt walked) [])))\n   496\t\n   497\t\n   498\t(defn load-index\n   499\t  \"Start loading the published index `manifest-address` names into the\n   500\t   node's local store; `step` advances it and reports `:loaded` or\n   501\t   `:load-failed`.  A load already started, loaded or failed is left as\n   502\t   it is.  Answers the node.\"\n   503\t  [node manifest-address]\n   504\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? manifest-address)\n   505\t    (throw (ex-info \"dao.space.dht/load-index takes a manifest address\"\n   506\t                    {:manifest manifest-address})))\n   507\t  (if (contains? (:loads node) manifest-address)\n   508\t    node\n   509\t    (assoc-in node [:loads manifest-address]\n   510\t              {:status :loading :fetching nil :fetched 0})))\n   511\t\n   512\t\n   513\t(defn load-status\n   514\t  \"`{:status :loading | :loaded | :failed ...}` for `manifest-address`, or\n   515\t   nil when no load was started: `:loaded` carries `:datoms` (the count)\n   516\t   and `:fetched` (blobs fetched from peers), `:failed` its `:reason`.\"\n   517\t  [node manifest-address]\n   518\t  (when-let [{:keys [status fetched datoms reason]}\n   519\t             (get-in node [:loads manifest-address])]\n   520\t    (cond-> {:status status :fetched fetched}\n   521\t      (= :loaded status) (assoc :datoms (count datoms))\n   522\t      (= :failed status) (assoc :reason reason))))\n   523\t\n   524\t\n   525\t(defn loaded-datoms\n   526\t  \"The EAVT datoms of a loaded index, or nil.\"\n   527\t  [node manifest-address]\n   528\t  (let [record (get-in node [:loads manifest-address])]\n   529\t    (when (= :loaded (:status record))\n   530\t      (:datoms record))))\n   531\t\n   532\t\n   533\t(defn- fail-load\n   534\t  [node m reason]\n   535\t  [(update-in node [:loads m] assoc :status :failed :reason reason :fetching nil)\n   536\t   [{::event :load-failed :manifest m :reason reason}]])\n   537\t\n   538\t\n   539\t(defn- advance-load\n   540\t  [node m done-by-id]\n   541\t  (let [{:keys [fetching], :as record} (get-in node [:loads m])\n   542\t        done (when fetching (get done-by-id (:id fetching)))]\n   543\t    (cond\n   544\t      (and fetching (nil? done)) [node []]\n   545\t\n   546\t      (and done (not (:found? done)))\n   547\t      (fail-load node m (str \"no peer produced \" (:address fetching)\n   548\t                             (when-let [why (or (:lost done)\n   549\t                                                (get-in done [:error :code]))]\n   550\t                               (str \" (\" why \")\"))))\n   551\t\n   552\t      :else\n   553\t      (let [fetched (cond-> (:fetched record) done inc)\n   554\t            node (update-in node [:loads m] assoc :fetching nil :fetched fetched)\n   555\t            walked (try {:datoms (index-datoms (probing (local node)) m)}\n   556\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   557\t                          (if-some [address (missing-in e)]\n   558\t                            {:missing address}\n   559\t                            {:error e})))]\n   560\t        (cond\n   561\t          (contains? walked :datoms)\n   562\t          [(update-in node [:loads m] assoc :status :loaded :datoms (:datoms walked))\n   563\t           [{::event :loaded :manifest m :datoms (count (:datoms walked))\n   564\t             :fetched fetched}]]\n   565\t\n   566\t          (:missing walked)\n   567\t          (let [{:keys [outcome id], :as asked}\n   568\t                (content.step/request-get (:client node) (:missing walked))]\n   569\t            (if (#{:requested :pending-request} outcome)\n   570\t              [(-> node\n   571\t                   (assoc :client (:state asked))\n   572\t                   (assoc-in [:loads m :fetching]\n   573\t                             {:id id :address (:missing walked)}))\n   574\t               []]\n   575\t              (fail-load node m (str \"could not ask for \" (:missing walked)\n   576\t                                     \" (\" (name outcome) \")\"))))\n   577\t\n   578\t          :else\n   579\t          (fail-load node m (str \"the index is invalid: \"\n   580\t                                 (or (ex-message (:error walked))\n   581\t                                     (str (:error walked))))))))))\n   582\t\n   583\t\n   584\t(defn- advance-loads\n   585\t  [node]\n   586\t  (let [loading (sort-by str (keep (fn [[m r]] (when (= :loading (:status r)) m))\n   587\t                                   (:loads node)))]\n   588\t    (if (or (empty? loading) (nil? (:dht node)))\n   589\t      [node []]\n   590\t      (let [{:keys [state completions]} (content.step/step (:client node)\n   591\t                                                           fetch-budget)\n   592\t            done-by-id (into {} (map (juxt :id identity)) completions)]\n   593\t        (reduce (fn [[node events] m]\n   594\t                  (let [[node more] (advance-load node m done-by-id)]\n   595\t                    [node (into events more)]))\n   596\t                [(assoc node :client state) []]\